/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  ed06_stages_in_series  --  FOUR electrodialysis stages in series, and why a
  plant steps the current DOWN along the train.

  THE NETWORK NEEDS NO ELECTRICAL TOPOLOGY, and that is the point worth
  stating first.  An ELECTRICAL STAGE is a set of cell pairs served by ONE
  electrode pair on its own rectifier.  So stages in series are simply UNITS
  in series: four `electrodialysisStack` units, each with its own
  `electricLoad` rectifier on its own energy wire, the diluate passing from
  one to the next and the concentrate loop passing through all four.  Nothing
  in the engine models a busbar, and nothing needs to.

  THE ARRANGEMENT.

      D0 --[ ST1 ]-- D1 --[ ST2 ]-- D2 --[ ST3 ]-- D3 --[ ST4 ]-- D4
      C0 --[      ]-- C1 --[      ]-- C2 --[      ]-- C3 --[      ]-- C4
             |             |             |             |
            R1            R2            R3            R4     (four rectifiers)

  Each stage is the industrial frame of `ed05_industrial_stack`
  (EurodiaED-100P-50: 100 cell pairs, 50 m2 of cell-pair area, 0.5 m2 each),
  and each is asked for `targetDemin 0.6` -- sixty per cent of ITS OWN inlet
  -- so the ENGINE solves the current every stage needs instead of the case
  declaring four numbers.

  WHAT THE RUN MEASURES (printed by this run; nothing here is a target):

      stage      I [A]      i [A/m2]    i_lim [A/m2]    i/i_lim
        1        26.80        53.60        338.88        0.158
        2        10.72        21.44        135.55        0.158
        3         4.29         8.58         54.22        0.158
        4         1.72         3.43         21.69        0.158

      overall demineralisation  97.44 %   (0.05 -> 0.00128 mol/kg)

  THE LESSON.  The limiting current is a PREDICTION from the diluate
  composition (Geraldes & Afonso, J. Membr. Sci. 360 (2010) 499-508), so as
  the diluate is stripped down the train i_lim falls with it -- 338.88 A/m2
  at the first stage, 21.69 A/m2 at the fourth, a factor of 15.6.  A plant
  therefore CANNOT hold one current density along the train: stage 1 runs at
  53.60 A/m2, and that same density in stage 4 would be 53.60 / 21.69 = 2.47
  times ITS limiting current -- deep in the water-splitting regime, with the
  current efficiency collapsing and the membranes stressed.  Running each
  stage at its own current keeps the same 0.158 margin everywhere, and the
  current falls by the same factor the inlet concentration does.

  This is the steady twin of `edbatch01_constant_current`: there ONE stack
  sees a falling concentration in TIME and crosses its own limiting current;
  here FOUR stacks see it in SPACE and each is given a current that suits
  where it sits.  A batch rig and a series train are the same physics read
  along two different axes.

  WHAT IS PINNED AND WHAT IS NOT.  The golden pins the answer this model
  gives.  Nothing here reproduces a measured four-stage plant; the stack
  record is Vitor Geraldes' own industrial unit as he remembers it (its own
  header says so, value by value) and its mass-transfer correlation is
  BORROWED from the bench stack and applied inside the Reynolds band it was
  fitted over.  The concentrate loop is CO-CURRENT and single-pass; no
  back-diffusion, no water transport and no inter-stage pumping are modelled.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

// stream state lives on disk in 0/ (per-stream files); flowsheetDict is TOPOLOGY only

units
(
    {
        name        ST1;
        type        electrodialysisStack;
        inputs      ( D0  C0 );
        outputs     ( D1  C1 );

        operation
        {
            stack             EurodiaED-100P-50;
            membrane          CMX_AMX;      // the record names no pair -- the CASE must
            targetDemin       0.6;          // each stage removes 60 % of ITS OWN inlet
            xi                0.9;
            E_electrodes      2.0;          // V (raw SI), lumped, announced
        }

        energyOutputs
        (
            { name power;  kind work;  expression "W_electric";  unit W; }
        );
    }
    {
        name        R1;
        type        electricLoad;
        operation   { eta 1.0; }
        energyInputs
        (
            { from ST1.power;  kind work;  target W_shaft; }
        );
    }
    {
        name        ST2;
        type        electrodialysisStack;
        inputs      ( D1  C1 );
        outputs     ( D2  C2 );

        operation
        {
            stack             EurodiaED-100P-50;
            membrane          CMX_AMX;      // the record names no pair -- the CASE must
            targetDemin       0.6;          // each stage removes 60 % of ITS OWN inlet
            xi                0.9;
            E_electrodes      2.0;          // V (raw SI), lumped, announced
        }

        energyOutputs
        (
            { name power;  kind work;  expression "W_electric";  unit W; }
        );
    }
    {
        name        R2;
        type        electricLoad;
        operation   { eta 1.0; }
        energyInputs
        (
            { from ST2.power;  kind work;  target W_shaft; }
        );
    }
    {
        name        ST3;
        type        electrodialysisStack;
        inputs      ( D2  C2 );
        outputs     ( D3  C3 );

        operation
        {
            stack             EurodiaED-100P-50;
            membrane          CMX_AMX;      // the record names no pair -- the CASE must
            targetDemin       0.6;          // each stage removes 60 % of ITS OWN inlet
            xi                0.9;
